From 81809ea366eacf4bb2c9459df5ee90b10a9d372c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luca Bruni <luca.bruni@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(rocr): invalidate the vector L1 in the gfx9 dxg
 ACQUIRE_MEM

The dxg thunk's gfx9 ACQUIRE_MEM only sets SH_KCACHE_VOL_ACTION_ENA. The
vector L1 (TCP) is per CU and not coherent with other CUs, so a kernel can
read stale lines left by an earlier kernel: wrong results, runaway kernels,
engine-reset storms and one 0x10E bugcheck on gfx90c.

Also set TC_ACTION_ENA, TCL1_ACTION_ENA and TC_WB_ACTION_ENA, matching the
Linux kernel driver's gfx9 mem sync (gfx_v9_0_emit_mem_sync).

Checked on gfx90c: 30-line repro; rocPRIM, rocThrust, hipFFT, hipDNN pass;
hipSOLVER 11746/11746 (before: 8095 failures plus resets); hip-tests no
regressions.
---
 projects/rocr-runtime/libhsakmt/src/dxg/wddm/cmd_util.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/projects/rocr-runtime/libhsakmt/src/dxg/wddm/cmd_util.cpp b/projects/rocr-runtime/libhsakmt/src/dxg/wddm/cmd_util.cpp
index 11cd812f30..ae1bb3eaa6 100644
--- a/projects/rocr-runtime/libhsakmt/src/dxg/wddm/cmd_util.cpp
+++ b/projects/rocr-runtime/libhsakmt/src/dxg/wddm/cmd_util.cpp
@@ -120,7 +120,13 @@ size_t CmdUtil::BuildAcquireMem(
     acq.acquire_mem.bitfields2.coher_cntl =
       (1 << 29) | // CP_COHER_CNTL__SH_ICACHE_ACTION_ENA_MASK
       (1 << 27) | // CP_COHER_CNTL__SH_KCACHE_ACTION_ENA_MASK
-      (1 << 28);  // CP_COHER_CNTL__SH_KCACHE_VOL_ACTION_ENA_MASK
+      (1 << 28) | // CP_COHER_CNTL__SH_KCACHE_VOL_ACTION_ENA_MASK
+      // The vector L1 (TCP) is per CU and not coherent with other CUs, so it must be invalidated
+      // before each dispatch or a kernel can read stale lines left by an earlier kernel. Matches
+      // the gfx9 mem sync in the Linux kernel driver (gfx_v9_0_emit_mem_sync).
+      (1 << 23) | // CP_COHER_CNTL__TC_ACTION_ENA_MASK
+      (1 << 22) | // CP_COHER_CNTL__TCL1_ACTION_ENA_MASK
+      (1 << 18);  // CP_COHER_CNTL__TC_WB_ACTION_ENA_MASK
     memcpy(pBuffer, &acq, sizeof(acq));
     ret = sizeof(acq);
   } else if (major >= 10) {
